egment offers power products to manage power requirements across various voltage levels, including battery-management solutions, DC/DC switching regulators, AC/DC and isolated controllers and converters, power switches, linear regulators, voltage references, multiphase controllers and power stages, and lighting products. This segment also provides signal chain products that sense, condition, and measure real-world signals and convert them into data to be transferred or converted for further processing and control, such as amplifiers, data converters, interface products, motor drives, clocks, and logic and sensing products. The Embedded Processing segment offers microcontrollers, processors, wireless connectivity, and radar products; and applications processors for specific computing activity. It also provides DLP products primarily for use in projecting high-definition images; calculators; and application-specific integrated circuits. Its products are used in various markets, such as industrial, automotive, personal electronics, communications equipment, enterprise systems, calculators, and others. The company markets and sells its semiconductor products through direct sales and distributors, as well as through its website. Texas Instruments Incorporated was founded in 1930 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","employees":33000,"website":"https://www.ti.com","country":"United States","city":"Dallas","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Haviv  Ilan","title":"President, CEO & Chairman"},{"name":"Mr. Amichai  Ron","title":"Senior Vice President of Embedded Processing & DLP® Products"},{"name":"Ms. Julie C. Knecht","title":"Senior VP, CFO & Chief Accounting Officer"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":18.39,"tpe":32.71,"ps":6.516,"pfcf":32.14,"peg":1.005,"pb":7.933,"rev_growth":0.215,"eps_growth":0.4515,"eps_growth_fwd":0.2552,"eps_growth_next":0.1933,"div_yield":0.0011,"roe":0.2323,"roa":0.07977,"de":47.91,"gross_margin":0.5924,"op_margin":0.225,"profit_margin":0.1914,"current_ratio":1.